{:id :g3-data-encrypted-at-rest
 :date "2026-10-25"
 :row :G3
 :claim "Data encrypted at rest: the data disk is written as AES-128-GCM ciphertext under a key held on the system ESP; reading the disk outside the OS shows only ciphertext."
 :host {:model "MacBookPro18,4", :cpu "Apple M1 Max", :os "Darwin 25.4.0 arm64"}
 :commit "7bcfbd73a0984b8c0af90c5e11bd7245dbc1042d"
 :verdicts {"key-created-and-carried" {:green? true, :reason :marker, :marker "AIUEOS_DATA_KEY_CREATED tsc-entropy weak (loader wrote \\EFI\\AIUEOS\\DATA.KEY and carried the key in boot-info v6)"},
            "storage-stack-through-encryption" {:green? true, :reason :marker, :marker "AIUEOS_VIRTIO_BLK_OK, AIUEOS_JOURNAL_OK, AIUEOS_KOTOBA_JOURNAL_PLAN_OK, AIUEOS_KOTOBA_OBJECT_WRITE_OK, AIUEOS_OBJECT_STORE_OK, AIUEOS_OBJECT_TXN_OK — the journal/object stack runs through the AES-GCM wrap (F1 non-regression)"},
            "records-are-ciphertext" {:green? true, :reason :offline-digest, :marker "external read of virtio-blk-smoke.img: plaintext record magics AIUECRS1 / AIUEOBJ / AIUEJRN all count 0"}}
 :run
 {:mechanism "every virtio-blk sector read/write is AES-128-GCM wrapped (sector-number nonce, key from boot-info v6); the GCM tag is discarded — integrity stays with the journal's record checksums, confidentiality from the cipher"
  :key-ownership "the key lives at \\EFI\\AIUEOS\\DATA.KEY on the system ESP, a different disk from the data volume it protects"
  :external-read "sha/raw scan of the data disk image after the boot run: no record magics, no readable record payloads"
  :markers ["AIUEOS_DATA_KEY_CREATED (uefi-debug.log)" "AIUEOS_JOURNAL_OK and the object-stack markers (kernel-serial.log)"]}
 :caveats
 ["the filesystem FORMAT superblock (AIUEFS1 at sector 0) is plaintext by construction — it is built host-side by make-aiuefs-image.py before the OS runs; all OS-written records are ciphertext"
  "the GCM tag is not stored (the sector is exactly 512 bytes): integrity comes from the journal's own record checksums, not the AEAD tag"
  "key entropy is the TSC (qualification source, documented weak); rotation/backup of DATA.KEY is an operational step — losing it makes the data unreadable"
  "owner may reject: 'read the disk from outside' is measured as a raw scan for record magics and payloads; a formal ciphertext-strength analysis was not done"]
 :green? true}
